  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "About thirty determinatives cover most words in Middle Egyptian texts. Learning them is the fastest way to guess what an unknown word is about. This lesson collects the most common ones; they build on <a href=\"/egyptology/middle-egyptian-1/determinatives/\">Determinatives</a>."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "The ones to know first: the seated man <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓀀</span>, the seated woman <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓁐</span>, the god <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓀭</span>, the walking legs <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓂻</span>, the man with hand to mouth <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓀁</span>, the papyrus roll <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓏛</span>, the house <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓉐</span>, the town <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓊖</span>, the hills <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓈉</span> and the water <span class=\"eg-h\" style=\"font-size:1.6em;line-height:1\">𓈗</span>."
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Sign",
